--- body ---
## Context

Child of 0700, first of the two moves promised to the editor. Identify the
field's main research currents, their publication venues, and their citation
lineages, on an identified revision of the v3 working corpus.

This is the part that carries the novelty argument: the field had only been
mapped on corpora of a few hundred to a few thousand documents. The 33,344
refined works and 1,087,209 citations are the benchmark of the published v2;
record the counts of the REL revision after the v3 additions.

## Actions

1. Check the DOI, then title, concordance of the Zotero/PDF references of the
   Gavard & Schoch audit against the current corpus; handle the relevant
   absences in the v3 pipeline before fixing the REL revision (0700).
2. Current detection on the REL revision — reuse what exists
   (`conception/clustering-comparison.md`, `clustering-validity-positioning.md`)
   rather than starting from scratch.
3. Publication venues per current, and their evolution by period.
4. Citation lineages: which works found which current, and through which
   relays.
5. Figures and tables in `deliverables/_shared/`, generated, never maintained
   by hand.

## Test

A detected current must be recognisable: a hands-on check of a sample of works
per current, read by the author. A partition whose classes cannot be named is a
partition to redo, not a result.

The concordance of candidate references must assign each Zotero record a
verifiable status: DOI present, duplicate established by title, included after
reconstruction, excluded by scope rule, or to be resolved. The REL
reproduction test recomputes counts, currents and tables from the recorded
commit, DVC pointers and window, without reading a more recent version.

## Invariants

- The v3 working corpus evolves; REL computations cite a commit, the DVC
  pointers and the analytic window. The v2 data paper deposit stays intact:
  different v3 counts are not an inconsistency.
- A reference found in Zotero but absent from the corpus is not used to
  measure presence or absence in the literature before its inclusion rule has
  been examined and the REL revision reconstructed.
- No analysis carried over from the Œconomia manuscript — see the guard in 0705.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Currents identified, named, and validated hands-on by the author
- [ ] Venues and lineages produced, with their generated figures
- [ ] Concordance of candidate references checked by DOI and title, with motivated exclusions and relevant absences corrected in v3
- [ ] REL corpus revision, window, counts and DVC pointers recorded;
      figures and tables reproduced from these inputs
